A||N||4||FieroMaster88||Really mad.......I want my car back!!!||||8||
Z||000000||FieroMaster88||05-12-2001||12:08 AM||||Ok, About 3 weeks ago someone tried to break into my car.  They broke a tail light and a sail window and broke up a lot of fiberglass.  The body shop told me they found all the parts and it would be 2 weeks to do the job (including installing the parts and painting the whole rear of the car).  Well, 2 days after i take it in, they call me and say they cant find the rain gutter strip and the 2 clips for the sail window.  Ok, thats no big deal, Fleabitdog sent me some (without me paying him yet).  I call this tuesday and he says the car will be done by thursday, call him thursday morning and set up a time to pick it up.  I call thursday morning and my car is still not painted and the tail light they ordered came in broken, but my car will be done by friday with a broken taillight but they will replace it when a new one comes in.  Ok, that would be cool.  Well, they call me back thursday before they close and the car is STILL NOT PAINTED!!!  But they found a tail light in arazona and it will be there monday and I will get the car back then......<P>Well, today he calls me and tells me they dont have a sail window for the passanger side now, their company that was gonna provide it fell through!  I will have to find one and put it in myself, but the car should be done monday!!!  Now I am really pissed.  <P>So I have 2 questions for everyone here.<P>One: What should I do about this???  This is a "professional" company (Carstar).  This is not good coustomer service.<P>Second: Does anyone have a MINT condition sail window they could sent me?  I need it badly and would love to have it before carlisle.<BR>N/m, FieroDave is awesome, he is sending me a sailwindow!!!<BR>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">          <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles    <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/smiling2.gif">   <P>[This message has been edited by FieroMaster88 (edited 05-12-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by FieroMaster88 (edited 05-12-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||thomas_l||05-12-2001||07:22 AM||||If it ain't done by Monday be prepared to drive it out. I got my wife's son's car into a paint & body shop for $800 worth of body work and metallic blue paint. This after we did $500 of hood, header panel, grille, etc. After it didn't get touched for a week, I showed up with my wife ready to drive it out and amazingly they had finally gotten started. Two days later we go to pick up and they did a real shitty job. Same cycle - a week of lies and delays, a threat to pull it, and they finally did it over. My usual behavior is two times nice guy then I become a complete bastard. I worked in automotive repair for 10 years so I know things happen and deadlines pass. I also know when somebody is trying to baffle me with BS  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000002||TWEETIE BIRD||05-12-2001||12:58 PM||||I got an estimate on my paint job and they told me I would have to wait a month, which I did. They told me they would have to have it a month. OK, so at the end of the month I call them to make arrangements to pick it up and they havn't even started it. I finally got it back after 9 weeks. The same thing happened with my engine rebuild. He told me it would take 2 weeks and it took 4 months. Always some kind of excuse, and then it cost $1000 more then he said. Needless to say, I will never recommend either place to anyone. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.ascenture.net/users/bhhum/fiero1.jpg"> ||||reg||8
Z||000003||kslish||05-12-2001||01:46 PM||||Hmmm, Carstar Auto Body....I once had an estimate for some body work done at Carstar.  One thing you'll quickly learn about national chains like this, the more expensive the job, the quicker it will get done.  They are more concerned about doing insurance work on new cars since they'll make more money at it.  When you try save some money, or if they have to search and find used parts (instead of just purchasing new ones from a dealer) they don't want to hear it.<P>I ended up taking my Fiero (the front end was pretty messed up after taking on a Toyota Camry) to a small independent.  It did take a month instead of the two weeks as originally quoted (he spent a lot of time cutting and welding in a repalcement frame member).  And the paint isn't absolutely perfect (better than the average Maaco job though)...but he impressed me by actually charging me LESS than originally quoted since he took so long.  Let's see one of these huge shops do that.  <P>I learned my lesson a while ago to usually go to a small reputable shop to have something done when needed.  They tend to not rush the work or make as many mistakes since they are concerned with doing the job right instead of just getting the car out the door.  They need the good word of mouth to get consistant business, so they tend to focus on customer service.<P>Just my 2 cents,<P>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||05-13-2001||04:46 AM||||I run into this all the time. In my shop, they way I do business, is I get all the parts first, then let the customer know. Then I dont take the job till Im actually ready to start it. Drop it off Sunday nite, the parts in the garage, and I start on it Monday morning. Work on only one car till its done. Everyones happy. Ill use fill in jobs or my own car during drying times. Im not a chain of course, but I dont have thousands of dollars lying around in parts at one time.||||reg||1
